ants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques\/contains(where:)"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques\/contains(where:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques"]]},"references":{"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/MaximalCliques/contains(where:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques\/contains(where:)","kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"contains"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:ST7ElementQa","text":"Element"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","text":"Bool"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"rethrows"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","text":"Bool"}],"url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques\/contains(where:)","title":"contains(where:)","type":"topic","role":"symbol"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/MaximalCliques":{"role":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every maximal clique of an undirected graph’s simple graph once, lazily, each in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order (by vertex index): an isolated vertex, or one whose only edges are loops, is a clique of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one. The order is Eppstein–Löffler–Strash’s: by the cliques’ first vertex in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"coreNumbers().degeneracyOrdering"},{"type":"text","text":", then as Bron–Kerbosch with Tomita’s pivot (ties to the least"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"index) and branches in ascending index meets them. The sequence holds the graph, so iterating"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"again gives the same cliques. O(n + m) before the first clique, O(d·n·3^(d\/3)) in all for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"degeneracy d."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MaximalCliques","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques","title":"MaximalCliques","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MaximalCliques","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques":{"role":"collection","type":"topic","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques","title":"Cliques","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/cliques"}}}